==Strategy==
This stage is relatively simple, only 2 Rain Ds and 2 Berserkories. [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] is required here, because Berserkory's waves will tear through your units. Long ranged Ubers or anti-red Ubers can easily destroy the Berserkories. It is possible to use a [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] to push the Rain D. behind the Berserkory, and permafreeze him using [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]]. Other than that, you just need to bring some high DPS units to destroy the Rain D.

Alternatively you can spam [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Dread Pirate Catley]] to knockback Berserkory back to the base and spam [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] to keep the Rain D's from destroying your Dread Pirate Catley stack.

If your units are leveled enough (level 40 Roe and Courier, Octopus doesn't matter), you can just spam [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]], Courier Cat, and Octopus Cat to vaporize Berserkory and by the time he dies, your Courier stack will be large enough to juggle the Rain D. behind the base and easily win the stage.

